{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.836,
   "text": "The house we bought came with one thing the old owners wouldn't take. A cardboard box in the attic."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.636,
   "end": 17.057,
   "text": "Taped to its lid was a note. Never close this box. And whatever ends up inside it... let it keep."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 18.057,
   "end": 22.089,
   "text": "I laughed. It was just a box, sitting open in the dust."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.889,
   "end": 27.775,
   "text": "A week later, my reading glasses went missing. I found them in the box."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.475,
   "end": 32.208,
   "text": "Then my watch. Then my keys. Then my wedding ring."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.108,
   "end": 38.633,
   "text": "Every time, I took them back. And every night, the attic floor creaked a little longer."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 40.833,
   "end": 43.799,
   "text": "So one night... I taped the box shut."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.999,
   "end": 49.713,
   "text": "The creaking stopped. For six days, the house was perfectly quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.913,
   "end": 55.479,
   "text": "Then my wife asked who I'd been whispering with in the attic every night."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 57.079,
   "end": 60.62,
   "text": "I went up. The tape was split... from the inside."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 62.02,
   "end": 67.524,
   "text": "The box was full. My shoes. My coat. Every photo of me... face scratched out."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 68.524,
   "end": 73.985,
   "text": "Downstairs, I heard my wife laugh... and say my name. To someone in the kitchen."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 75.585,
   "end": 79.703,
   "text": "I've been up here for a while now. She hasn't noticed I'm gone."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 80.703,
   "end": 83.903,
   "text": "And the box keeps telling me... there's room."
  }
 ],
